# Reference Point — Main Section Display (`h2.display`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for a main section headline (e.g. "Choosing between Chatbot VS Inline AI", "Reimagining Discovery…"), match base `h2.display` — **not** the italic comparison variant.

## Structure

```html
<header class="ai-compare-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">The AI trust layer</p>
  <h2 class="display">Choosing between Chatbot VS Inline AI</h2>
  <p class="lead">Supporting sentence under the display head.</p>
</header>
```

Also used as:

```html
<div class="stack-24">
  <p class="eyebrow">Section label</p>
  <h2 class="display">Main section headline</h2>
</div>
```

Pair with brown `.eyebrow` above. Optional `.lead` below.

## Visual spec

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `h2.display` (base class) |
| Font | `var(--serif)` → Instrument Serif |
| Size | `var(--display)` → **clamp(2.25rem, 4.4vw, 3.5rem)** |
| Weight | **400** |
| Style | **Regular** (not italic); use `<em>` for phrase emphasis only |
| Color | `var(--ink)` → **#1a1a1a** |
| Line-height | **1.1** |
| Letter-spacing | **-0.01em** |
| Margin | 0 (global reset) |

## Base CSS

```css
.display {
  font-family: var(--serif);
  font-size: var(--display);
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.1;
  color: var(--ink);
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}
```

Canonical live example: `#ai-layer` → `.ai-compare-head` → `h2.display` (“Choosing between Chatbot VS Inline AI”).

Other matches (same treatment via scoped selectors):

```css
#discovery > .stack-24 > h2.display,
#post-purchase > .stack-24 > h2.display,
#guardrails > .stack-24 > h2.display,
.ai-compare-head h2.display
```

Also: Overview section head.

## Wrapper (AI compare)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Wrapper | `.ai-compare-head` |
| Layout | column flex, `gap: 24px` |

## vs other headlines

| Class / element | Use |
|-----------------|-----|
| **`h2.display` (base)** | **Main section heads — regular serif, `--display`, `var(--ink)`** |
| `h2.display` in `.comparison-head` | Comparison pin — **italic**, `--ink-deep`, line-height 1.15 — see `reference-point-comparison-display.mdc` |
| `h3.title` in `.overview-sub-head` / `.hybrid-chat-head` | Subsection heads — smaller `--title-sm` |
| `.title` (h2) | Mid-level heads (e.g. What's next) — `--title`, not `--display` |

## Do not

- Apply italic to the full line — that is the **comparison** variant only.
- Use `var(--ink-deep)` for base section displays — base uses `var(--ink)`.
- Shrink to `--title` or `--title-sm` — collapses hierarchy against subsection titles.
- Confuse with `.ai-compare-card-title` — card titles are a separate component.
